WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.430
Two great facts and a book to

2
00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.890
cite — in ten seconds!

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.160
Lesson planning done.

4
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.180
But one fact is wrong.

5
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.800
And the book doesn’t exist.

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.210
Today: check before you trust.

7
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.470
How can that happen?

8
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.690
A chatbot writes one

9
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.150
likely word at a time.

10
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.460
It learned which words usually come next

11
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.360
from huge amounts of text — like your

12
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.700
phone keyboard, on a much bigger scale.

13
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.750
But it learned how sentences sound, not

14
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.750
which facts are true: its training text

15
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.570
had no ‘true’ or ‘false’ labels.

16
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.960
For a rare fact, like a date or a

17
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.520
book title, it may guess — and the

18
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.440
guess sounds just as sure.

19
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.520
Many tests of chatbots even reward

20
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.480
a guess over ‘I don’t know’.

21
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.450
This is called a hallucination: an answer

22
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.350
that sounds sure but is false or made up —

23
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.650
a fact, a quote, even a book.

24
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.340
The AI isn’t lying on purpose.

25
00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.770
It’s predicting, and

26
00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.310
predictions can be wrong.

27
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.860
In 2023, US lawyers cited six

28
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.600
court cases a chatbot had

29
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.760
invented — and stood by them.

30
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.240
One even asked the chatbot if a

31
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.100
case was real — it said yes.

32
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.980
They were fined five thousand dollars.

33
00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.330
By October 2026, over two thousand

34
00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.350
court decisions worldwide had

35
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.050
found AI-made-up content.

36
00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:33.770
Quick check!

37
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.370
My chatbot sounded very sure.

38
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.110
Its answer is probably right…

39
00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.140
isn’t it?

40
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:41.960
Not necessarily.

41
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.090
Sounding sure isn’t being right — chatbot

42
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.750
makers warn about this themselves.

43
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.280
But in a 2026 trial, a warning

44
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.260
label didn’t change how much

45
00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.080
medical students relied on AI.

46
00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.540
So let’s build a habit.

47
00:01:58.860 --> 00:01:59.820
Here’s the habit.

48
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.640
Ask clearly — never put pupils’

49
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.800
names, marks, phone numbers or

50
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.700
photos into an AI tool.

51
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.210
Check important facts in a trusted

52
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:12.650
source: Mr Okafor’s atlas confirms the

53
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.210
chatbot’s fact about the Nile, but not

54
00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.570
its fact about Lake Victoria: three

55
00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.730
countries share the lake.

56
00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:19.850
And the book?

57
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.620
He can’t find it anywhere.

58
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.840
Then decide: keep, fix or drop.

59
00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.270
Experts do the same.

60
00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.510
A mobile money company in Kenya says

61
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.170
investigators review what its fraud AI

62
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:34.750
flags.

63
00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.170
AI that reads chest X-rays for TB

64
00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.090
only flags who might be ill — a

65
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.230
lab test must confirm.

66
00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.150
One flood forecast service says its

67
00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.650
forecasts are for information only.

68
00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:49.630
Your turn.

69
00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.690
Which request is safe to

70
00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.110
type into an AI tool?

71
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.680
The quiz — no pupils’ details.

72
00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.590
Remember: AI can be useful, but it

73
00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.870
predicts; it doesn’t check facts the

74
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.250
way a careful person does.

75
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.590
So ask clearly, check what

76
00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.310
matters, then decide.

77
00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.770
You’re the teacher; the AI is a tool.

78
00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.600
Try it in class tomorrow: read five

79
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.660
statements in a robot voice — one is made

80
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:20.800
up.

81
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.440
Pupils vote for the fake and say

82
00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.420
how they’d check: textbook,

83
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.940
teacher, library or an elder.

84
00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.610
End with Ask, Check, Decide.
